==German==

===Etymology===
From (late and northern) {{inh|de|gmh|schal|t=tasteless, turbid}}, borrowed from {{der|de|gml|schal}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*skal-}}, derived from {{der|de|ine-pro|*(s)kelh₁-||to dry out}}. Compare {{cog|sv|skäll|t=thin, weak, bleak}}, {{cog|ang|sceald|t=shallow, flat}}, whence modern {{cog|en|shallow}} and {{m|en|shoal}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃaːl/}}
* {{audio|de|De-schal.ogg|Audio}}
* {{homophone|de|Schal}}

